<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>thrift</id>
    <version>__VERSION__</version>
    <title>Apache Thrift Compiler</title>
    <authors>Apache Thrift Developers</authors>
    <owners>Apache Software Foundation</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://thrift.apache.org/</projectUrl>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/apache/thrift</projectSourceUrl>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/apache/thrift/tree/master/build/windows/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://thrift.apache.org/docs/</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/THRIFT</bugTrackerUrl>
    <mailingListUrl>https://thrift.apache.org/mailing</mailingListUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <iconUrl>https://thrift.apache.org/assets/images/thrift-logo.svg</iconUrl>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) The Apache Software Foundation</copyright>
    <tags>apache thrift rpc idl codegen compiler serialization admin</tags>
    <summary>The Apache Thrift IDL compiler</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
Apache Thrift is a software framework for scalable cross-language services
development. It combines a software stack with a code generation engine to
build services that work efficiently between a large number of languages.

This package installs the Thrift compiler, which turns a `.thrift` interface
definition into client and server code. The runtime libraries are distributed
separately, through each language's own package manager.

The package downloads the Windows installer from the Apache archive and runs
it. The installer adds the compiler to `PATH`, so open a new shell afterwards.

## Notes

* This is the compiler only, not a runtime library.
* The download is verified against a SHA-256 checksum recorded in this package.
* Apache Thrift releases are voted on by the Apache Thrift PMC. The official
  release artifact is the source tarball; this package is a convenience build.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/apache/thrift/blob/master/CHANGES.md</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <!-- The compiler links the shared runtime, so it needs the Visual C++
           redistributable, which the ASF cannot ship. Chocolatey installs
           this first. -->
      <dependency id="vcredist140" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
